      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · Dyczkowski pp.65–81 (source-matched transcript); the quilt's sleeper correction",
          "title": "The Śaiva genealogy: measure, dream, crystal",
          "italic": "The veil embodies manifestation's own power — not an alien substance across a finished spectator; the dream carries the same forgetting intimately.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The Śaiva passage gives the opening a genealogy. Anuttara/Paramaśiva names the unobjectifiable ground; Śakti is its power of manifestation and self-articulation — prakāśa and vimarśa belonging together as luminosity and reflexive awareness. Māyā brings measure: this appears, that is withheld; the kañcukas give the bounded knower effective terms — kalā, vidyā, rāga, kāla, niyati. Paśu names the bounded position; puruṣa and the inner instrument articulate an inhabitable field: buddhi determines, ahaṃkāra appropriates, manas coordinates. The veil belongs to manifestation's power — not an alien substance thrown across an otherwise finished spectator. The dream carries",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "the pressure intimately: while dreaming, the fact of sleep can disappear from the experienced situation; waking changes the objects' relation to their condition without making the urgency something that never occurred. Taylor's explicit sleeper correction appoints dissociation, tattvic contraction and the slash to the same event in the ontological register — a substantive authorial identity, not proof the cosmos sleeps. The crystal makes a different limit visible: a polished surface can display a landscape without knowing the display; in the Śaiva account the mirror of consciousness also generates and hosts its appearances — no machine phenomenality established.\n\nOccurrences: the kañcukas and paśu (#1, returned at #4's correction); the dream's forgotten condition (#1, #2); the crystal's unknowing display (#1, distinct from #2's usurpation).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
