      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#4–#5→0 · the eightfold field; the Neumann appointments (human-amplified: yes); the Arbitration field at register 3",
          "title": "Recognition returns through the veil",
          "italic": "The return keeps the world differentiated and the knower situated: līlā's play has real positions and consequences — the return releases their claim to originate the whole, not the positions themselves.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The whole's native articulation is the complete field: parent −/−; 0/1; ?/!; −/+; X/x; AM/IS; ∞/dx; returning 1/0 — the page's six turns renumber nothing. The Neumann appointments carry En-Soph and tohu-bohu at −/−, world-parent separation at 0/1, coming to light at ?/!, hunger at −/+, ego against ground at X/x, the \"I am\" at AM/IS, the round's Mono/Poly fullness at ∞/dx, descent and return at 1/0 — human-amplified: yes as the author's full-field amplification. The paśu correction is decisive: in the p.105 passage recognition precedes separation into husband and wife; the bounded position arises within recognition's field and cannot retrospectively originate it. The toroidal",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "appointment keeps its exact offices: Anuttara/Paramaśiva retains the unobjectifiable opening; Māyā is the measure-field wound around it — calling Māyā the hole would remove its positive work and put measure where it cannot enclose. Recognition returns through the veil: \"Līlā veils; hybris absolutises the veil; recognition sees the veil as Śakti.\" A24 receives the consequence — necessary measuring and usurped measure require different responses; A19 the complex's changed jurisdiction; A04 contextual seeing; A21 resituation without deleting the differentiated life; A27 the Other not reducible to a place in my image; A35/A36 the completed view returning to the zero it could never occupy.\n\nDeclared cross-story: toroidal offices shared with the uroboros whole; the paśu correction shared with the Neumann whole. ↳ Occurrences: the veil and the opening (#1, #4, #5→0); the eye opening again (#0, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
